{
  "_comment": [
    "The closed corpus this server speaks. Text is authored here once and",
    "recorded once per voice by `record.py`; every WAV IS committed, so a clone",
    "can hear the avatar without fetching a speech model — see that script and",
    "server/README.md.",
    "",
    "Two voices, because the avatar has a gender and the voice has to agree with",
    "it. `vql_speech` is the real id — what `--tts vql-speech` asks Voqalize's own",
    "service for. `piper` is the stand-in that keeps `--tts canned` free of every",
    "credential: a licence-clean local model recorded into `audio/<voice>/`.",
    "Choosing a voice picks the whole row, so the two backends can never disagree",
    "about which one is speaking.",
    "",
    "22050 Hz is piper's native rate for these voices, not a choice. Resampling",
    "to 24 kHz here would add a dependency and a lossy step to reach a number",
    "nothing needs: pipecat's output transport resamples to the transport rate",
    "anyway (base_output.py, `_resampler.resample`).",
    "",
    "Sentences are split the way TTSService aggregates them, because that is how",
    "they arrive at synthesis — one `run_tts` call each. Keep them short. This",
    "avatar listens far more than it speaks, and a backchannel that lands is",
    "worth more here than a paragraph that does not."
  ],
  "sample_rate": 22050,
  "default_voice": "female",
  "voices": {
    "female": {
      "label": "Female",
      "vql_speech": "omnivoice/gauri",
      "piper": "en_US-ljspeech-high",
      "piper_licence": "public domain (LJSpeech)"
    },
    "male": {
      "label": "Male",
      "vql_speech": "omnivoice/gaurav",
      "piper": "en_US-joe-medium",
      "piper_licence": "CC0 (OHF-Voice joe)"
    }
  },
  "lines": [
